{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.numerators_of_abel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.numerators_of_abel","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L292-L318","doc":"**Abel's five-term relation at three points, plus reflection at four, gives\nthe level-7 numerators `(17, 5, -1)`.**\n\nThe five-term hypotheses carry their own arguments — `x * (1 - y) / (1 - x * y)`\nand the rest — so nothing about which instance is which is assumed here; that is\nwhat `arg_A1` … `arg_C2` prove. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hC_of_five_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hC_of_five_term","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L253-L272","doc":"**`hC` from the five-term instance** `x = w₂`, `y = s`.\n\nIts denominator `1 - x·s` collapses to `x` (`hC_denom`), which is why the fourth\nargument reduces to `1 - s` outright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hB_of_five_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hB_of_five_term","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L231-L251","doc":"**`hB` from the five-term instance** `x = 1 - w₂`, `y = q`.\n\nIts denominator `1 - (1-x)·q` collapses to `q` (`hB_denom`), which is why the\nfifth argument reduces to `x` outright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hA_of_five_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hA_of_five_term","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L217-L229","doc":"**`hA` from the diagonal five-term instance** `x = y = w₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L211-L215","doc":"`q = 1/(2-x)` forces `q` to be a unit: at `q = 0` the relation reads `0 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.bloch_key'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.bloch_key'","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L194-L198","doc":"`bloch_key` in the `w₂` generator: `(1-x)²(1+x) = x²` for any root of the\ncubic. Identical to `FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.bloch_key`; restated here so the\nconnection to `arg_C2` is a `linear_combination` and not a comment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_C2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_C2","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L166-L188","doc":"**`arg_C2`**: the fifth argument. `s(1-x)/x = 1-r`, division-free as\n`(1-r)·x = s(1-x)`.\n\nThis is `bloch_key` again: clearing `r = x/(x+1)` and `s = (1-x)/x` turns it into\n`x² = (1-x)²(1+x)`, exactly\n`QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.bloch_key`. The identity that made the Bloch\nelement `2[w] + [-w]` work is the same one that fixes `hC`'s last argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hC_denom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hC_denom","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L160-L164","doc":"**`hC`'s denominator collapses**: `1 - x·s = x`. The reason the fourth\nargument `x(1-s)/(1-x·s)` is exactly `1-s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_C1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_C1","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L155-L158","doc":"**`arg_C1`**: the third argument, `x·s = 1-x`. This is the *defining*\nrelation of `s`, so it is free — and it makes `hC`'s denominator `1 - x·s`\ncollapse to `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_B2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_B2","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L138-L151","doc":"**`arg_B2`**: the fourth argument. `(1-x)(1-q)/q = 1-s`, stated division-free\nas `(1-s)·q = (1-x)(1-q)`. This needs the minimal polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hB_denom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.hB_denom","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L131-L136","doc":"**`hB`'s denominator collapses**: `1 - (1-x)·q = q`. Immediate from `arg_B1`,\nand the reason the fifth argument `q(1-(1-x))/(1-(1-x)q) = q·x/q` is exactly\n`x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_B1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_B1","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L126-L129","doc":"**`arg_B1`**: the third argument, `(1-x)·q = 1-q`. True for every `x`; and it\nis what makes `hB`'s denominator `1 - x·y` collapse to `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_A2","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L118-L122","doc":"**`arg_A2`**: the fourth and fifth arguments coincide at the diagonal, and\n`x(1-x)/(1-x²) = x/(1+x) = r`. Note this is true for **every** `x` — the cubic\nplays no part. Stated division-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_A1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.arg_A1","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L108-L116","doc":"**`arg_A1`**: the third argument. `x·y = x²` at the diagonal, and it equals\n`1 - q`. This needs the minimal polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.ne_zero_of_hs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.ne_zero_of_hs","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L99-L104","doc":"`s = (1-x)/x` already forces `x` to be a unit, with nothing else assumed: at\n`x = 0` the relation `s·x = 1-x` reads `0 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.two_sub_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.two_sub_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean#L93-L97","doc":"`q = 1/(2-x)` forces `2 - x` to be a unit. ","signatureChunk":0}]}